    <briefdescription>
<para>The image identity block every production STM32 image carries (#362). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>32 bytes, little-endian, at a fixed offset from the app&apos;s start (IDENTITY_OFFSET). The bootloader (#363) checks it at every boot and before it commits an update; the Gateway uploader (#366) and the client (SkyHawkClient#177) read it from an image file before anything is sent. The shared linker script (Firmware/shared/stm32f103.ld) places the block; Firmware/shared/osh_image.py fills in imageLength and imageCrc after linking. Everything else is set at compile time.</para>
<para>The block is defined by the role library — <ref refid="namespacePanelGroup" kindref="compound">PanelGroup</ref>, <ref refid="namespacePduNode" kindref="compound">PduNode</ref>, <ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref> — with its NodeKind, through <ref refid="FirmwareImage_8h_1af12054619552aca4fabb7187c07aaa65" kindref="member">OSH_FIRMWARE_IDENTITY()</ref>. A sketch without a role has no block. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
